From: davtur19 <davtur19@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Re-apply the client geometry after a DPI change in setGeometry

QWindowsWindow::setGeometry() computes the native window rectangle from the
requested client rectangle and the full frame margins of the window's current
screen. If the requested geometry is on a screen with a different DPI, the
window is moved there by MoveWindow() and Windows recalculates the non-client
area for the new DPI, while the window rectangle was built with the frame
margins of the old DPI. The client area then ends up offset and resized by the
frame delta; the wrong geometry is saved and restored again on the next start.

handleDpiChanged() does not apply the suggested rectangle for a DPI change
caused by setGeometry(), because Windows would scale the already scaled size
once more. It must still update the frame margins and re-apply the requested
client geometry, otherwise every cross-DPI setGeometry() leaves the client
area at the wrong place.

After the move, if the window DPI changed, recompute the full frame margins
for the new DPI and apply the requested client rectangle again.

Pick-to: 6.11
---
 src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowswindow.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowswindow.cpp b/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowswindow.cpp
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowswindow.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowswindow.cpp
@@ -2335,8 +2335,18 @@
         // achieve that size (for example, window title minimal constraint),
         // notify and warn.
         setFlag(WithinSetGeometry);
-        setGeometry_sys(toFullScreenGeometry(rect));
+        const auto dpiBefore = savedDpi();
+        const auto fullScreenRect = toFullScreenGeometry(rect);
+        setGeometry_sys(fullScreenRect);
         clearFlag(WithinSetGeometry);
+        if (savedDpi() != dpiBefore) {
+            // The window ended up on a screen with a different DPI, so the
+            // window rect above was computed with the frame margins of the
+            // old DPI. Re-apply the requested client geometry with the
+            // frame margins of the new DPI.
+            updateFullFrameMargins();
+            setGeometry_sys(fullScreenRect);
+        }
         if (m_data.geometry != rect && (isVisible() || QLibraryInfo::isDebugBuild())) {
             const auto warning =
                 msgUnableToSetGeometry(this, rectIn, m_data.geometry,
